  "readme": "# Quaternius Fantasy Props MegaKit - ordinary prop selection\n\n11 unmodified original FBXs: one crate, barrel, bench, stool, rope coil, closed\nbook, bottle, pot, peg rack, workbench and wall shelf. No combat/fantasy items.\nOriginal source: https://quaternius.com/packs/fantasypropsmegakit.html\nOriginal download: https://quaternius.itch.io/fantasy-props-megakit\nAuthor: Quaternius. CC0 1.0 Universal; exact License_Standard.txt retained.\n\nThe simple wood faces and everyday silhouettes fit the Paper Theatre harbour,\nworkshop and house references. Limit changes to the reference palette, paper\nsurface, small scale/pivot corrections and texture relinking. The source texture\nsets used by these models are retained, including the creator's alternate Unreal\nnormal maps. Their source material slots are documented in SOURCE.json.\n\nThe street lantern, open ledger, bell, plant and hoist remain explicit gaps. The\ncage-like wall lantern was omitted because it does not match the defining street\nlantern silhouette closely enough. Creator previews and metadata were inspected;\nAll 11 FBXs passed a separate Blender 5.2.2 LTS background import with no\nunresolved referenced texture images after original-image relinking. Eight\nrepresentative stock-material renders were inspected. Book and bottle source\ncolour attributes survive import, but their FBX material graphs do not connect\na vertex-colour shader node; inspect that connection when preparing a derived\nworking material. The stool seat is round. Source bytes and hashes remain\nunchanged. UE 4.27.2 import/render verification remains pending.\n",
  "retrieved_utc_date": "2026-10-14",
